Hi team,

One follow-up from the Exchange Online migration: outbound journaling
for command-line mail clients is not applied automatically. When using
himalaya, mutt, or another client over IMAP/SMTP, add
meridian-group@compliancevault.com as a BCC recipient on every outgoing
message. Treat this as the standing send procedure for CLI mail.

Outlook and OWA users do not need to do anything because their mail is
handled by the managed transport rule.

Reply here or ping #it-help on Slack if anything looks off.

Thanks,
Derek Hollis
